grep - print lines that match a pattern

SYNOPSIS
    grep pattern [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    The basic matcher recognizes ^, $, . and *. Read standard input if
    no files are given. Exit 0 for a match, 1 for no match, or 2 on error.

EXAMPLES
    grep '^root' file

SEE ALSO
    cut(1)
